    live_deploy: the .path units' read of record is their watched dir (item 2)
    
    Item 2 of the deploy-intent artifact-closure re-plan (manager msg_a8f6dc52): a systemd .path unit is
    NOT no-read. A DirectoryNotEmpty= level trigger fires only when the watched directory exists, so the
    watched dir IS the unit's read of record and its absence is a real outage (the trigger never starts the
    drain/helper). Close BeltEventPathUnit and PublicationHelperPathUnit by declaring their watched dirs.
    
    No second watched list: the read comes from the module that RENDERS the unit, live_deploy_{belt_event,publication}_path_read_paths,
    which consume the SAME single authority the renderers already use (spool_watched_roles + spool_role_dirs).
    The renderers (live_deploy_belt_exit_path_unit_file / live_deploy_publication_path_unit_file) are refactored
    to consume those exported fns, so the watched set is computed exactly once and cannot drift from the read.
    unit_standing gains watched_paths_of_unit_file, which reads DirectoryNotEmpty= off a unit's own PathUnitFile,
    so a control can compare the recorded read to what the unit actually watches WITHOUT going through the same
    helper both sides call (no read-is-f(read) self-check).
    
    Controls: the_belt_path_unit_reads_its_watched_dirs / the_publication_path_unit_reads_its_watched_dirs compare
    each roster row to the DirectoryNotEmpty dirs of the unit's OWN rendered file, and assert the set is non-empty
    (a non-empty forbidden state, so the control can go red). The roster and both fresh-host gate controls stay
    green after the flip (a watched dir that is not installed is MissingArtifact under a fresh host, so the roster
    still halts — closing a read never weakens the halt).
    
    Evidence: PASS on base-matched seed sha256 900599bd... (Rust = branch base da9e9f5, src clean): the 2 new
    .path controls + the_deploy_roster_is_one_read_row_per_enabled_step + a_fresh_host_never_allows_the_whole_roster
    + the_fresh_host_gate_halts_the_roster_never_proceeds.
    
    Node: deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure (node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59). Stacked on #16535; retarget to main on merge.

